# A spell on the stack is itself the object a text-changing effect changes (CR 612.1), so it resolves with its changed text -
# unlike an ability, whose text is fixed as it is put on the stack (CR 113.7a). Bot1 casts Glimpse the Core's first mode
# ("search your library for a basic Forest card") and in response Magical Hack replaces Forest with Island in the spell's text:
# it searches for a basic Island. The Forest in the library is not offered; the Island is found, and enters tapped.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Glimpse the Core
Magical Hack
Plains
Plains
Forest
Island
Swamp x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Glimpse the Core.Cast
Bot1.Modes(1)
Bot1.Choose(Close mana window)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Magical Hack.Cast(Stack.Glimpse the Core)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Forest)
Bot1.Modes(Island)
! Bot1.Search(Forest)
Bot1.Search(Island)

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Glimpse the Core; Magical Hack
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Island; Mox Jet; Mox Sapphire
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Tapped = true
Bot1.Library.Count = 12
